WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Ductwork is where most systems lose efficiency. Learn to read it and you'll find
problems other techs miss.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Full-length Type III practice exam. 25 questions covering low-pressure systems,
chillers, purge units, water contamination, and rupture discs.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Type III is often the section students
struggle with most because they have less hands-on experience with chillers.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: Low-pressure systems operate below atmospheric. And — Purge
units remove air that leaks IN

00:02:24.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

